      "statement": "SessionSandboxEventProcessor routes validated sandbox events to family handlers (streaming, artifacts, execution, runtime, push), owns cross-family concerns (one clock reading, one message-attribution resolution), and sends the ack for a critical event only after its handler finishes so unacknowledged criticals are safely re-delivered; the execution handler settles execution_complete by projecting message status, releasing the queue, broadcasting, firing notifyComplete, and triggering a snapshot.",
