      "id": "claim_50633e9e2a8b40eaa0e7fa1390ea8656",
      "statement": "On bridge disconnect, the DO's disconnect handler ignores closes for replaced sandbox sockets, skips termination when the sandbox status blocks reconnect, and otherwise awaits reconnect and schedules a lifecycle check (snapshot-restore respawn), while the bridge's forwarder recovers its buffered and unacknowledged-critical backlog on the next bind — the session's persisted pending/processing messages live in the DO so restored sandboxes re-attach and queued prompts dispatch.",
